{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/566161-jonathan-strange-and-mr-norrell-airing-on-bbc-america","id":566161,"title":"Jonathan Strange and Mr. Norrell airing on BBC America","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-24T01:06:53-07:00","id":566161,"title":"Jonathan Strange and Mr. Norrell airing on BBC America","content":"It started airing last week, a couple of weeks behind the BBC. The title characters are mages, but the antagonist, The Gentleman with the Thistledown Hair, is the main inspiration for C:tL's Gentry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T01:24:20-07:00","id":566186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/566161-jonathan-strange-and-mr-norrell-airing-on-bbc-america#post566161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The title characters are mages</div> </div> </div> </div>In personality yes. In magic style they're actually using a non-flexible system like Sin-Eater Ceremonies, built on top of a pact-magic system that they never really make use of.<br /> <br /> You could do them in the WoD quite easily. All spells must be brought as rotes/Ceremonies and have set Yantars. No improvised magic, and modifying spell factors requires an Intelligence + Occult roll before casting and changes the Yantras. New rotes can only be learned from books, other Mages, or brought from a Patron (WoD Summoners has the rules; patrons should be Spirits, but friendlier and without the predation theme).<br /> <br /> I think that would get everything they did in the books; except Strange's very early experiments (which were mostly inferior to learning from books anyway)<br /> <br /> <br /> The Gentleman is portrayed rather differently in the BBC and book version; both variants would make a great Gentry.<br /> <br /> And it's good - really really good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-24-2015, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/cor